as we get closer and closer to apple's  march event we are getting new  information about the three max the  apple is going to release and today we  have some bad news the very original  first leaker of the notch for the 14 and  16 inch macbook pros just gave us new  information that the laptop that we are  expecting in the march event that has  been filed with the ecc  looks to be a base model macbook pro  that is going to retain the same 13-inch  design and screen  now personally we here at max tech have  three issues  with this leak but it could be correct  and then we also have three possible  scenarios on why and how apple would  decide to stick with this machine but  first let's go ahead and take a look at  the sleek from somebody that is close  with apple's supply chain they are  saying that we are going to get the m2  processor which is kind of what we are  expecting that's the most likely  scenario but this machine will have the  same exact display the same size  everything identical including the touch  bar yes the touch bar  and all the only change is going to be  that it will have the m2 chip now with  that m2 chip that will be an upgrade and  that will help this macbook still sell  along with the lower price of course  compared to the 14 and 16 inch macbooks  as you guys know we have not been  recommending anybody to buy the m1  macbook pro just because the macbook air  is such a nice device for 300 less msrp  and actually an even greater discount  once you factor in the amazing prices on  amazon that we have seen as low as  850 dollars now yes this macro pro does  have a fan does have a little bit more  performance especially under extended  loads but we did not think that the  extra was worth it and because of that i  think this is probably the worst selling  laptop right now so if apple goes ahead  and upgrades that processor they are not  only going to increase the performance  of the cpu just by a little bit they  will also increase the efficiency the  battery life will be even better but the  graphics is going to jump all the way to  maybe a nine and a ten core  configuration uh instead of you know the  seven and eight core options that they  have right now with that m1 chip so this  has is gonna have a little bit more  graphics performance and it definitely  is going to help out there now even  though this is a possibility our first  issue is that apple is putting a brand  new chip into a very old design that  doesn't really match up with what their  future is holding right we have mac safe  now we have more ports we have no touch  bars they gave us a full-size keyboard  in the 14 and 16-inch macbook pros with  large function keys and then this would  be them just saying hey we're gonna hold  this old design which is not our future  that seems a bit odd now the second  issue that we have is that as soon as  the macbook air that's going to be  redesigned and likely launching in the  fall comes out this is going to be the  last machine that holds this old design  it's going to make it even older and of  course that is also going to get the m2  chip as well so this would give this  laptop a usable kind of lifespan of  about six months before it just feels  even more outdated and left in the past  that will just make it irrelevant that's  gonna really tank its value and it's  just kind of an odd decision now the  third issue that we have with it is that  if apple does keep this old design they  are not going to be able to raise the  price point from its current base 1299  up to say 1399 or 1499 which is what we  expected if they will go ahead and use  the 14-inch chassis and then maybe  remove some of the options we've seen  lately when apple has released their new  macbooks they've raised the price when  they released the imax they also raised  the price and they're adding new  features they're making them nicer but  in general prices are going up and apple  definitely cannot release the same  macbook with just a new chip and raise  the price more so and that also will  affect the redesigned macbook air that's  going to come out in the fall because if  this machine is still priced at 12.99  it'll be tough for them to price the new  macbook  much higher than this or even the same  price it has always been lower than the  macbook pro so if this first scenario  does come to be true  i guess the benefit is for apple it will  kind of guide more people to spend more  money if they want the new redesign with  the notch with the pro motion display  the sd card reader hdmi with magsafe it  really is going to push people to spend  more money it's going to make that 2 000  price point seem like a better value and  along with that if the scenario comes  true then the leaks from mark german  that came out previously will also be  correct but he said that it could be the  old design but without the touch bar  which this new leak is saying the touch  part is still here now scenario number  two could be an m2 chip coming out but  with the 14 inch new design from the  macbooks that came out last fall this is  personally what we were expecting and  what we think would be better because  it's going to future proof this laptop  and they could price it at 1500 dollars  and remove some of the features that  come with the 2 000 14 inch macbook pro  it would be very similar to that but it  would come with slower ssds so instead  of up to 7  400 megabit per second it will stick  with the standard kind of 3 000 megabyte  per second range it's going to have  slower ram it's going to come with less  ram instead of 16 gig down to 8 also  half the ssd 256 gigabyte to start and  it would also likely come with worse  speakers compared to the six speaker  setup if we look into the past this is  exactly what happened with the base  macbook pro it would look very similar  spec wise but when we actually did tests  the ssd would be slower some other  components would be slower and even  though speakers weren't advertised they  were significantly  worse sounding and then the higher end  model so you did get the extra when you  paid for it and with the previous 13  inch macbook pros once you upgraded the  256 gigabyte and 16 gigs of ram from the  base model you are only one hundred  dollars away from the higher end for  thunderbolt port model and in this  scenario if they do price at 1500 that  will result to the same exact kind of  layout that they have done for many  years now the third scenario could be  that it will be very similar to the one  i just talked about but they could also  take away some of the ports for example  they could take it with the hdmi they  could take away the sd card reader and  take away one of the thunderbolt ports  so cleave that side clean and then on  the other side you still have two ports  there like we did in the past and then  you also have the magsafe charger as  well so you kind of have a little bit  more options than the previous 13 inch  macbook pro now of course that would  suck but like apple's done in the past  the base macbook pros did have more  limitations and less ports than if you  bought the more expensive one but you  guys let me know what are your thoughts  do you think they will really release  the same 13-inch macbook pro with the  touch bar but just with the m2 chip and  if so is that enough to get you to  actually buy one of those machines  instead of spending more on the 2 000 14  inch or waiting for the fall for a  redesigned macbook air i want to hear  your opinions down below click that  circle above to help us reach 1 million  subscribers thanks for watching this has  been max check out one of those great  videos right over there and i'll see you  in the next video  [Music]

